{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>The ra'ah and the ayah.</b> It is the ra'ah, it is the ayah, it is the dayah. And why is it called ra'ah? Because it sees most keenly. And why does Scripture warn with all its names? So as not to give an opening to a litigant to argue — lest the one who forbids it call it ra'ah, and the one who comes to permit say, 'This one's name is dayah,' or 'Its name is ayah,' and this one Scripture did not forbid.' And regarding birds, He enumerated for you the impure ones, to teach that the pure birds are more numerous than the impure; therefore He enumerated the fewer (Ḥullin 63)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:02.823845247Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}